ent-AshWalkerHearth = stone hearth
    .desc = A basalt-lined hearth. Feed the coals timber or pressed fungal boards, then lay food or scraped hides on top.
ent-AshWalkerSoil = ash garden bed
    .desc = Fertile ash held by stones. Plant seeds or spores, water it and compost spare produce.
ent-AshWalkerMortar = basalt mortar and pestle
    .desc = A stone mortar and pestle for grinding mushrooms and fruit into juice.
ent-AshWalkerSeedSieve = spore sieve
    .desc = A porous fungal bowl for separating viable spores and seeds from fresh produce.
ent-AshWalkerMushroomBowl = mushroom bowl
    .desc = A bowl pressed from tough fungal fibres. Holds 50 units of water or medicine.
ent-AshWalkerMushroomLantern = ember mushroom lamp
    .desc = A living ember stem nestled in a fungal bowl. Its steady glow needs no fuel.
ent-LavalandBasaltBoulder = basalt boulder
    .desc = Weathered basalt. Break it with a pickaxe to obtain building stone.
ent-WallAshWalkerBasalt = basalt wall
    .desc = Closely fitted basalt blocks protect the settlement from beasts.
ent-DoorAshWalkerBasalt = basalt gate
    .desc = A heavy stone gate bound with sinew. It opens by hand.
ent-ClothingBackpackAshWalkerCrafted = hide satchel
    .desc = A roomy satchel sewn from dried goliath hide and watcher sinew.
ent-MaterialFungalWood3 = pressed fungal timber
    .desc = Tough polypore fibres pressed into light boards. Suitable for building and fuel.
ent-MaterialFungalCloth2 = woven fungal cloth
    .desc = Soft cloth woven from polypore fibres.
ent-FloorTileAshWalkerStone4 = basalt floor tiles
    .desc = Stone tiles for the settlement's floors.
ent-MaterialBasalt1 = basalt blocks
    .desc = Pieces of stone for walls, hearths and other structures.
ent-MaterialAshWalkerLeather1 = cured goliath leather
    .desc = Hide scraped clean and dried over the coals. Ready for sewing.
ent-AshWalkerScrapedHide = scraped goliath hide
    .desc = A cleaned, still-damp hide. Dry it over the hearth.
ent-FoodLavalandPorciniCooked = roasted porcini leaf
    .desc = A hearty mushroom leaf browned over the coals.
ent-FoodLavalandInocybeCooked = roasted inocybe cap
    .desc = Thorough cooking has driven the toxins from this mushroom cap.
ent-AshWalkerWoundDressing = fungal wound dressing
    .desc = A crushed porcini leaf bound in fungal fibres. Soothes bruises and open wounds while slowing bleeding.
ent-AshWalkerBurnDressing = cactus burn dressing
    .desc = Cool cactus pulp wrapped in a fleshy mushroom leaf. Eases heat and acid burns.
ent-CrateAshWalkerFarming = ash walker farming crate
    .desc = Lavaland spores and seeds, a sieve, a mortar, bowls, lamps and gardening tools.
ent-LavalandPolyporePlant = ash polypore
    .desc = A hardy plant of the ash wastes. Regrows after harvesting.
ent-LavalandPolyporeWild = ash polypore
    .desc = A wild plant rooted in fertile ash. Ripe produce can be harvested by hand.
ent-LavalandPolyporeSeeds = ash polypore spores
    .desc = Plant these in an ash garden bed.
ent-FoodLavalandPolypore = polypore shavings
    .desc = Tough fungal fibres for boards, cloth, bowls and dressings.
ent-LavalandPorciniPlant = leafy ash mushroom
    .desc = A hardy plant of the ash wastes. Regrows after harvesting.
ent-LavalandPorciniWild = leafy ash mushroom
    .desc = A wild plant rooted in fertile ash. Ripe produce can be harvested by hand.
ent-LavalandPorciniSeeds = leafy ash mushroom spores
    .desc = Plant these in an ash garden bed.
ent-FoodLavalandPorcini = porcini leaf
    .desc = A fleshy mushroom leaf. Roast it for food or use it in dressings.
ent-LavalandInocybePlant = inocybe mushroom
    .desc = A hardy plant of the ash wastes. Regrows after harvesting.
ent-LavalandInocybeWild = inocybe mushroom
    .desc = A wild plant rooted in fertile ash. Ripe produce can be harvested by hand.
ent-LavalandInocybeSeeds = inocybe mushroom spores
    .desc = Plant these in an ash garden bed.
ent-FoodLavalandInocybe = inocybe cap
    .desc = A toxic raw mushroom cap. Roast it thoroughly over the hearth before eating.
ent-LavalandEmberPlant = ember mushroom
    .desc = A hardy plant of the ash wastes. Regrows after harvesting.
ent-LavalandEmberWild = ember mushroom
    .desc = A wild plant rooted in fertile ash. Ripe produce can be harvested by hand.
ent-LavalandEmberSeeds = ember mushroom spores
    .desc = Plant these in an ash garden bed.
ent-FoodLavalandEmber = ember stem
    .desc = A glowing stem. Its juice is rich in iron; a living stem can light a lamp.
ent-LavalandCactusPlant = ash cactus
    .desc = A hardy plant of the ash wastes. Regrows after harvesting.
ent-LavalandCactusWild = ash cactus
    .desc = A wild plant rooted in fertile ash. Ripe produce can be harvested by hand.
ent-LavalandCactusSeeds = ash cactus seeds
    .desc = Plant these in an ash garden bed.
ent-FoodLavalandCactus = cactus fruit
    .desc = A juicy fruit rich in water and vitamins. Its cool pulp soothes burns.
